				<note nid="n18033012.12">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">
				Why do 
				<crossref let="z" cid="c18033013.25">
				</crossref>
				you contend, 
				<crossref let="a" cid="c18033013.26">
				</crossref>
				against him, saying, ‘He will answer none of man’s(1) words’?(2)
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">
				For God 
				<crossref let="b" cid="c18033014.27">
				</crossref>
				speaks in, 
				<crossref let="c" cid="c18033014.28">
				</crossref>
				one way, and in two, though man does not perceive it.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">
				In a 
				<crossref let="d" cid="c18033015.29">
				</crossref>
				dream, in, 
				<crossref let="e" cid="c18033015.30">
				</crossref>
				a vision of the night, when deep sleep falls on men, while they slumber on their beds,
