				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">
				He has 
				<crossref let="d" cid="c18033028.55">
				</crossref>
				redeemed my, 
				<crossref let="e" cid="c18033028.56">
				</crossref>
				soul from going down into the pit, and my life shall look upon the light.’
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033029">
			</marker>
			<v n="29">
				“Behold, God 
				<crossref let="f" cid="c18033029.57">
				</crossref>
				does all, 
				<crossref let="g" cid="c18033029.58">
				</crossref>
				these things, twice, three times, with a man,
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033030">
			</marker>
			<v n="30">
				to bring 
				<crossref let="h" cid="c18033030.59">
				</crossref>
				back his, 
				<crossref let="i" cid="c18033030.60">
				</crossref>
				soul from the pit, that he may be lighted with the light of life.
				<note nid="n18033030.30">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v18033031">
			</marker>
			<v n="31">
